   {
    "id": "p_00040",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Since after the call to [I90]fclose[/I90]() any use of [I91]stream[/I91] results in undefined behavior, [I92]fclose[/I92]() should not be\nused on [I93]stdin[/I93], [I94]stdout[/I94], or [I95]stderr[/I95] except immediately before process termination (see XBD [A96][I97]3.287 Process Termination[/I97][/A96]), so as to avoid triggering undefined behavior in\nother standard interfaces that rely on these streams. If there are any [A98][I99]atexit[/I99]()[/A98]\nhandlers registered by the application, such a call to [I100]fclose[/I100]() should not occur until the last handler is finishing. Once\n[I101]fclose[/I101]() has been used to close [I102]stdin[/I102], [I103]stdout[/I103], or [I104]stderr[/I104], there is no standard way to reopen any of\nthese streams.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I90": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I91": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I92": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
